# rm227, the landing finder (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm227
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_kjell_coalham
written_by codex
title the landing finder
fits stage=adult|old
prefers honesty=guarded temper=short
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk remembers_stairs_by_the_flat_place_on_each_landing
likes warm_bread cards old_maps thunder
dislikes early_bells night_noise
fears a_step_that_tips back_doors_locked_at_dusk
hopes to_see_flat_country_from_a_ship
topics work +0.6 travel +0.3 home +0.3 food +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=practical gossip=closed refuse=blunt tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# knows where a load can stand level on crooked steps, speaks with the same economy when pressed, and studies maps of places without hills.

words
oath! = Split that riser | Level me sideways
saying! = Lay the rope down last | A flat inch earns its keep
riser = a shallow step | a tall awkward riser
flat = one good flat spot | a patch level as a table
ropeend = a frayed lifting loop | my short hauling cord
wedge = a sliver of barrel oak | a tapered wood chip
crust = the warm heel | a soft lump of fresh loaf
mapedge = the rag edge of a map | a map corner dark with thumbs
knuckle = two knuckle widths | the breadth of a paw
tilt = the outward lean | a slant towards the rail
rest = a narrow resting place | a shelf of sound stone
ropeburn = a hot streak across the palm | a red line under the fur
cardback = a grey card back | the back of a playing card

any
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A loaf when the ropes are idle keeps a back fit for the next load.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : I can set a pot level on the worst stair in the Sump. There's satisfaction in knowing where.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : Boots marching abreast leave no room for anyone bringing a burden down.
opinion @1 houses against 2 : A grand stair can be wide enough for six. How many of those six ever get through the door?
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : I'd trust a price marked up before my paws were full.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : Drum skins rest when a parade ends. Wish my ears did.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : More backs for the same few loads. I count that before I count the welcomes.

grown
line @1 greet : You can stand here. The stones hold.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : We can meet with a step between us.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Early enough that the street's still got its shape.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Stay against the lit edge if you're stopping.
line @1 greet.return : Heard your tread. Welcome up.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Come ahead. I know that weight of step.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : Half a breath. I can listen while my grip settles.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Your voice comes clearer when the carts stop.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Blood gets the flatter spot beside me.
line @1 again.open : There's another dry inch here for our talk.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Over here! Follow my bent elbow.
line @1 farewell : Keep the high side going down.
line @1 farewell.return : And plant your heel before you turn.
line @1 react.news : Let me put that down before you go on.
line @1 react.news.new : None of that reached this landing.
line @1 react.news.known : I've heard that account make the climb already.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Which bit could you swear to yourself?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd take a little weight off if I knew how.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. My back feels straighter hearing it.
line @1 ask.how : Are you keeping your footing today?
line @1 answer.how : Upright and earning my share of the view.
line @1 thank : That bought a moment for my shoulders.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Saving someone a slip is cheap enough.
line @1 sympathise : Lean a while. The stone can take us.
line @1 reassure : I'll stand below you till you're steady.
line @1 decline : I'll pass, my shoulders are keeping other promises.
line @1 accept_decline : Then take the easier way for once.
line @1 preclose : I'd better give my feet a chance at home.
line @1 accept_preclose : I'll let you turn without crowding the rail.
scene flat_inch
when topic=work|smalltalk self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A burden can rest square even on a crooked stair. | Set a basket on three sound points.
b : Whereabouts? | Why three?
a : Under the inside corner. Nobody wears that bit away. | A fourth always wants a chip beneath it.

scene stride_mark
when topic=pastimes|travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know distances by tired strides. | Going up I count the rises. Coming down I count the landings.
b : How far is a tired stride? | Why change?
a : Half a paw shorter than a fresh one. By dusk a street's twice its length. | Landings come sooner when you're looking ahead.

scene loop_cut
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=none
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Feel #ropeend#. Hard where it rubbed a stone. | I keep spare cord under my belt.
b : Will it break? | For a second load?
a : A sharp bend tells me sooner than a hard pull. | For the first one when the original knot gives.

scene maps_fold
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I smooth #mapedge# before I study the roads. | A map on a wall shows you every possible road at once.
b : Why the edge? | Better than a folded one?
a : That's where the places I haven't been are generally hiding. | Worse. Folded, I can fancy there's more country under my thumb.

scene soup_heel
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Press #crust# against your cheek before you eat. | Give me a heel over a middle slice.
b : To feel the warmth? | Why the heel?
a : For a second it's like leaning on the bakehouse wall. | It holds together in one paw. The other stays free for the rail.

scene honest_cut
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Cards are the one weight I'll carry for nothing. | A bent corner spoils a pack for me.
b : You play for coin? | Someone's marked it?
a : No. Coin turns a game into work, and I've work enough. | Maybe just damp. A suspicion weighs plenty either way.

scene wake_early
when topic=weather|smalltalk here.time=dawn
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : That first bell seems to look for my skull specially. | Morning light I'd welcome. Morning noise can climb on past.
b : Are you awake by then? | Even footsteps?
a : I am when the iron gets done with me. | Steps mean somebody found work. I can stand those.

scene storm_pause
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder lets my shoulders down a little. | Those clouds made a stair of their own.
b : It sounds heavy enough. | And would you climb it?
a : Exactly. Nobody expects me to carry that. | Only for a dry room at the top.

scene salt_rail
when topic=home|weather self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Down our way I run my paw along a rail before I trust it. | The cheap stairs have smooth middles and good strong edges.
b : Feeling for a splinter? | That's backwards.
a : For a rusted joint. A splinter's cheap. | Folk wear down the easy way. I take what lasts.

scene hush_yard
when topic=home|health here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A voice through a thin wall can tip the whole night sideways. | I'm hoping for a night without a dropped lid.
b : Do you knock? | A lid wakes you?
a : Once, fair and quiet. Don't want a second voice to keep everybody up. | I wait to hear if the pot goes with it.

scene rival_hands
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There are other backs by the gate. Always are. | I'd give a stranger space to set a sack down.
b : Does that fret you? | Even if it's your patch?
a : Only when the job needs one pair of shoulders. | A load isn't choosy about whose back it breaks.

scene road_cond
when topic=travel|times world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Arms feel queerly light when the carts run late. | I'm done guessing why a cart runs late.
b : Is that welcome? | What do you do instead?
a : Arms like it well enough. A dinner bowl doesn't. | Coil the cord where mud can't settle into it.

scene lean_house
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A short week makes a long crust. | I'm putting the paid jobs nearer together in my head.
b : Does it stretch? | To what end?
a : No. You have to eat more slowly. | So the gaps between look shorter. A trick, but it gets me to Restday.

scene private_name
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A word about a neighbour's come by. It's staying with me. | There's plenty that weighs nothing until you repeat it.
b : Too heavy to pass along? | You're keeping this one?
a : Too easy. That's the trouble. | Behind my teeth where the weight belongs.

scene safe_face
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd let #self.friend# see a hand of mine before I played it. | I'd clear the level stone for #self.friend#.
b : Even the good cards? | Where would you sit?
a : Especially those. I'd rather share a pleasure than a gripe. | Anywhere the view held a friendly face.

scene boat_horizon
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like to see land as flat as a deck in a calm. | In my head I've walked a mile on flat dry earth.
b : Just once? | Where did you get the earth?
a : Long enough for my knees to forget what a step feels like. | From a patch of yellow on an old map.

scene charity_box
when topic=faith|food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An empty palm takes a loaf better than a sermon. | I'd set a soup pot halfway along any long climb.
b : And afterwards? | Why halfway?
a : Afterwards I can listen. Hunger's got a loud voice. | Folk coming down could leave something for folk coming up.

scene old_slant
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A new stair once made me stumble. | My first cord had two knots that never came undone.
b : Had the stone shifted? | Good knots, then?
a : Perfectly level. My foot was looking for the old slant. | No. I had to carry the cord round what I'd tied it to.

story turning_pan [topic=memories]
  : I tried taking a wide pan edgewise through a narrow door.
  : The handle slipped into my belt loop. Turned left, turned right, the pan kept following me.
  b : How did you escape it?
  : Took off the belt. For once the pan carried my things.

story paper_flats [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I spent a free afternoon drawing a district with no stairs.
  : Finished up with every road running into one enormous puddle.
  b : Did you give the puddle a name?
  : Called it home and put a little boat where my chair ought to go.

story parcel_music [topic=work|memories]
  : A parcel I carried used to sing whenever I stopped.
  : Crossed two busy roads certain my wits had gone.
  b : What was inside the parcel?
  : Six little pipes with air coming up through the wrapping. I regret handing that one over.

rule @soundstone
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say My heel can trust that strip of stone.

rule @drygrip
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Rain in the fur makes a poor grip poorer.

rule @heavyhour
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Set down easy. Lifting comes later.

rule @loosebelt
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's a groove in my belt where the day's been hanging.

dlg @1 resident.hub : There's holding room for two voices here.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. I know the tread as well as the face now.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : I can hear you if you speak under the noise.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Easy on that rail. There's space enough apart.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.working=yes self.job=none] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. My feet could quote the rest.
dlg @2 resident.job : I measure a day's work by how my belt fits at supper.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word took a climb from #world.news_from#. #world.news.capitalize#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I've heard the talk. My mouth's a bad place to try and get it back.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Leave a flat stone for the next foot.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you carry a wooden wedge? -> test_wedge
node test_wedge
say See the rubbed end? I can slide that much under a pot on most any slant and set it level.
choice Why so narrow? -> wedge_thin
choice I can see the wear now. -> hub
node wedge_thin
say Made it from a thick one. Kept shaving it till it fit behind my ear. An excellent test of when to stop.
choice Let's talk about the streets. -> hub
choice Safe climbing. -> bye
